@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain
title Appending to a student's comment

box Logic LOGIC_COLOR_T1
participant ":LogicManager" as LogicManager LOGIC_COLOR
participant "c:CommentCommand" as CommentCommand LOGIC_COLOR
participant "r:CommandResult" as CommandResult LOGIC_COLOR
end box

box Model MODEL_COLOR_T1
participant "m:Model" as Model MODEL_COLOR
participant "p:Person" as Person MODEL_COLOR
participant "existing:Comment" as Existing MODEL_COLOR
participant "updated:Person" as Updated MODEL_COLOR
end box

note over LogicManager, CommentCommand
  Parsing is omitted. CommentCommandParser has already built c,
  holding the index, the new Comment, and isReplacing, which is
  false for c/ and true for c-/.
end note

[-> LogicManager : execute("comment 3 c/asks good questions")
activate LogicManager

LogicManager -> CommentCommand : execute(m)
activate CommentCommand

CommentCommand -> Model : getFilteredPersonList()
activate Model
Model --> CommentCommand : lastShownList
deactivate Model

note right of CommentCommand
  Rejected with a CommandException before anything changes:
  an index past the end of the displayed list, and c-/ on its
  own when the student has no comment to clear.
end note

CommentCommand -> Person : getComment()
activate Person
Person --> CommentCommand : existing
deactivate Person

CommentCommand -> Existing : lengthAfterAppending(comment)
activate Existing
Existing --> CommentCommand : combinedLength
deactivate Existing

alt combinedLength > Comment.MAX_LENGTH
    CommentCommand --> LogicManager : throws CommandException
    note over CommentCommand, Existing
      The student keeps their current comment.
    end note
else within the limit
    CommentCommand -> Existing : append(comment)
    activate Existing
    Existing --> CommentCommand : updatedComment
    deactivate Existing

    CommentCommand -> Person : withComment(updatedComment)
    activate Person
    create Updated
    Person -> Updated
    activate Updated
    Updated --> Person
    deactivate Updated
    Person --> CommentCommand : updated
    deactivate Person

    note right of Person
      Person and Comment are both immutable, so append and
      withComment return new objects rather than changing p.
    end note

    CommentCommand -> Model : setPerson(p, updated)
    activate Model
    note right of Model
      The displayed list is not re-filtered, so the indexes
      the TA sees stay stable.
    end note
    Model --> CommentCommand
    deactivate Model

    create CommandResult
    CommentCommand -> CommandResult
    activate CommandResult
    CommandResult --> CommentCommand
    deactivate CommandResult

    CommentCommand --> LogicManager : r
end
deactivate CommentCommand

[<-- LogicManager
deactivate LogicManager
@enduml
